### Footer Call to Action

Include a strong contact or consultation call to action that clearly explains the next step, links to the contact or consultation page, remains usable on mobile, uses strong contrast, and avoids generic wording.

### Footer Form

Where a mini inquiry form or newsletter form is included, keep it concise, use visible labels, include validation, include accessible status messages, maintain sufficient contrast against the dark background, and do not duplicate the complete contact form.

## 06. Brand Voice and Style

### Brand Personality

The brand should feel technical, precise, premium, polished, calm, trustworthy, practical, confident, modern, experienced, clear, reliable, and led by senior engineering judgment.

Avoid an exaggerated startup tone, vague marketing language, bloated corporate wording, or unnecessary jargon.

### Writing Style

Use clear, direct, benefit-focused copy.

The writing should use confident expert language, explain business outcomes, demonstrate technical credibility, emphasize risk reduction, emphasize implementation quality, emphasize maintainability, explain long-term business value, and clearly communicate what each service solves.

Headings should be crisp and specific.

Supporting copy should explain why the service matters, what problem it solves, how the company approaches the work, what the client receives, what business outcome the system supports, and how the completed system will remain maintainable.

Avoid filler language that could apply to any company.

### Content Density

Use detailed service-page copy with strong conversion sections, realistic project examples, clear deliverables, practical technical detail, business-focused explanations, credible implementation language, relevant frequently asked questions, and clear next steps.

The content should include enough technical specificity to feel credible to founders, operators, and technical buyers without becoming unreadable to a nontechnical business owner.

### Content Quality Rules

Every major section must have a clear purpose.

Do not repeat the same paragraph across multiple pages, reuse identical service copy, create empty cards, use generic “innovative solutions” language, make unsupported performance claims, display fake awards, display fake client logos, present fictional businesses as verified clients, use meaningless statistics, leave visible Latin filler copy in business sections, or create buttons that do not lead anywhere.

Realistic fictional project examples may be used, but they must be presented as portfolio-style examples rather than verified claims involving real clients.

